invariant: INV-17
file: rsa_sign64.c
catches: rsa_sign_equiv_test
reason: rsa_sign64_power returns without the wipe below its body, so the table
  of the base's sixteen powers and the slots the compiler kept words in
  stay in the stack.
  bin/rsa_sign_equiv_test requires no two words of a value the call held
  in the stack below it, and requires the stack equal under two secrets
  (docs/decisions.md 181).

--- old
    power_window(o, base, e, e_len, mod, 0);
    rsa_sign64_wipe_below();
--- new
    power_window(o, base, e, e_len, mod, 0);
